==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*3 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Awakened Bahamut Cat (Enemy)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The strategy for this stage revolves around abusing Awakened Bahamut Cat's backswing. To do this, you will want to lure Awakened Bahamut Cat, specifically within 100 range of him hitting your base, so that the last part of his [[Explosion]] spawns outside of your base while you continuously send out fast meatshields ([[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] is recommended) to permanently stall him. The main difference between Awakened Bahamut Cat and [[Raging Bahamut Cat]] is the aforementioned backswing, so you can sneak a [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] in between his attacks to deal chip damage over time. If that proves too difficult, a sufficiently leveled Thunderbolt Cannon can be used to artificially create such an opening or expand upon an existing one.

The biggest threat here will be the Shibalien Elites, whose sole purpose is to mess up your timing and ruin your run. Thanks to the huge magnification of 2300%, they are surprisingly bulky with 161,000 HP, but not to the point where they last long enough to where another one spawns before the current one dies. A level 50 [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] can take out around half of their health, leaving the rest to be taken out by a quick [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]] strike. If your cats' levels are not high, you can either use a Research [[Cat Combo|Combo]] or an Attack Up Cat Combo. Level 40 Maglev and Slime Cat is enough, make sure to cycle your Slime twice to deal enough damage for the Shibalien Elites to die (spawn Kitty of Liberty and Bullet Train Cat together if you use a Research Combo). Do not be scared to let the Shibalien Elites hit your [[Cat Base]] if you absolutely need to, but do beware this stage is balanced around CotC 3 completion, so players should max all the [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from every [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapter.

Alternatively, you can use [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] to knock back and slow Bahamut. Combined with meatshields, Bahamut can be effectively stalled as other units catch up.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: Fishman has a 7f window to get a hit off while Awakened Bahamut Cat is in his backswing and after an Explosion. This opening can increase to 11f when its Move Speed Up Talent is maxed out. Additionally, the opening window where you can send Fishman to hit Awakened Bahamut Cat may increase the closer he is to your base up, allowing you to have up to 26f without his Move Speed Up Talent and 28f with his Move Speed Up Talent when Awakened Bahamut Cat is currently attacking your Cat Base. Fishman may also be able to knockback Awakened Bahamut Cat in 2 hits if you have a maxed [[Sky Fruit]] [[Treasure]] and Fishman is at level 43 or at level 38 with a fully invested Attack Buff Talent.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Boulder Cat is by far the best meatshield here, since with 3 Research Sm [[Cat Combo]]s it can stall Bahamut on its own. Beware that the Shibalien Elites can push forward in the downtime between Boulder Cats.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]]: Sadako Cat is one of the few Cats who can withstand Awakened Bahamut Cat's damage, even just for a little bit. It is highly recommended to unlock its [[True Form]], Octopus Cat, as while its attack rate is slower than Sadako Cat's, Octopus can become tankier through its Defense Buff [[Talents|Talent]]. This unit works best with Sniperpunk strats, where you're going to keep Bahamut away for as much as possible.
*[[Mummy Sumo (Super Rare Cat)|Mama Mummy Sumo]]: Mama Mummy Sumo is another Cat that can withstand Awakened Bahamut Cat's damage, on top of having faster speed and higher health than Sadako Cat. Beware that she costs more compared to Sadako Cat and might waste all of your money gained from the Mooths.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]/[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Both are crowd-controllers who greatly outrange Awakened Bahamut Cat, making fighting him much easier. If using them, it's highly recommended to fight away from the Cat Base because of their low health and Cyberpunk's blind spot. However, if you're able to stack them up before Bahamut can get to them, the constant slow and knockbacks will effectively win you the stage.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train is the perfect unit for rushing in between Awakened Bahamut Cat's attacks and getting off chip damage (or stop Bahamut from reaching the base) due to its very high speed. Its Evolved Form, Maglev Cat, also works, though as a result of slower speed, True Form is still slightly better for easier timings.
*[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]]: Can be used to slip in between Bahamut's attacks to stall while your damage dealers come off cooldown. Note that Manic Eraser needs to be at least level 46 to tank a hit from the last explosion from Bahamut.
*[[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|The Kitty of Liberty]]: Unlike many other midrangers, this one has a low cooldown, short foreswing and decent damage for his cost and good enough range to keep the Shibalien Elites at bay by chipping them. At level 42 or higher, he can tank the last blast of Bahamut's Explosion, making timings much more lenient.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]]: Capable of surviving a few hits from Awakened Bahamut Cat, but its [[Multi-Hit]] and Explosion can shred his health easily.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: Can be used to push Awakened Bahamut Cat back instantly if he ever reaches or gets too close to the Cat Base, as well as dealing a large amount of chip damage. When Bahamut is at a safe distance, Supercar may also be used as damage against the Shibalien Elites, just enough to exceed half a Shibalien's HP (81,000) without any Attack Up Cat Combo if exactly at the max level of 50 (or with, if at any lower level, since a Shibalien may barely survive an extra hit without a Combo, but that doesn't really stop us from winning anyway).
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Another great source of chip damage with fast speed and a Wave Attack that can strike both Bahamut and any Shibalien Elite coexisting at a time. With direct bite and Wave combined, it deals the same damage as a Supercar Cat at the same level (if the direct bite doesn't knock the target back and make Wave miss). Therefore, Jelly Dumpling and Supercar can two-shot a Shibalien Elite alone with both at level 50 (with Jelly Dumpling attacking first so its direct bite doesn't knock Shibalien Elite back and halve its damage).
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Can take chunks of health out of the enemy Awakened Bahamut Cat and Shibalien Elite in case of an emergency push or finishing them off when you know they're about to die. You'll need to time his attack very carefully because the enemy Bahamut can kill yours in one hit, both from his direct attack and the following explosions.
*[[Inky Cat (Special Cat)|Inky Cat]]: They have Explosion Immunity. At Lv.35, or Lv.31 with a small Defense Up [[Cat Combo]], they can survive one hit from a Shibalien Elite. paired with Manic Eraser Cat, they hold the line pretty well, to where you can safely use Cyberpunk Cat and Sniper the Deadeye to slowly push back Bahamut and Shibaliens Elite without much issue. Please note that they are currently only available in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], for now.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
''Note that many of the [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] mentioned (specifically, the ones that can outrange Bahamut's Explosions) work better with Sniperpunk strats and less with [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Heavenly Tower Floor 30]]-style cycle strategies, as players would generally find it beneficial to preserve as much firepower as possible.''
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Lunacia is one of the few [[:Category:Cats with Explosion Immunity|units that are Immune to Explosions]]. She doesn't target [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], but can still deal great damage to Awakened Bahamut Cat. She can also deal with the Shibalien Elites very well, being Strong against them and Freezing them. A good idea to use in tandem with her counterpart.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Death's Daughter Lunacia]]: Unlike her [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] counterpart, she outranges Bahamut less, but she targets Floating instead of Alien and inflicts Weaken, allowing your units like Octopus Cat to live much longer, whilst also dealing serious damage to Bahamut. She might struggle against the Shibalien Elites a little, but her damage is enough. Using her with her counterpart allows them aid each other fairly well with all threats in the stage.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]]: He is tanky against Floating and Alien, has immunity to Warp and Explosions, Strengthens at half health for even higher damage and has an extremely low cooldown to where he can be sent even before the one on the field dies, and has a powerful conjure to help kill Shibalien Elite and profit a little more thanks to the conjure's Double Bounty effect. However, he is rather pricey and can drain your wallet if you aren't careful and Knockback can be a detriment by resetting Bahamut's backswing. Overall, a very powerful pick for this stage if you can work around his two weaknesses.
*[[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Rex]]: Even with their really low stats, the free Uber Rare can be found useful here as the Explosion Immunity allows it to ignore Bahamut's pierce. Their own attack cycle occasionally lines up to hit Shibalien, and their Savage Blow chance (although low at 15%) can deal extreme damage to Bahamut. Be ready to use your Iron Wall/Slowbeam when they attack, as if Giga-Nyan knocks Bahamut just as he does an explosion, Bahamut will rebound and hit again with no space for sending units, killing Giga-Nyan or hitting your base.
*[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]]: Filling a similar niche to Fishman Cat but with MUCH higher damage in return, speeding the battle up. Survive won't do it any good if he gets directly hit by Awakened Bahamut, as the Explosion's lingering hitbox will hit Yukimura again, essentially wasting the Survive. Survive instead allows him to still get a hit in if you mess up your timing and accidentally send him directly towards an Explosion.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Insanely tanky (969,000 HP at Lv. 30) versus Floating enemies, she's able to take a lot of damage from Awakened Bahamut and deal insanely high damage in return (118,830 DPH at Lv. 30), alongside having a low enough cooldown to be sent immediately after the other one dies. Do note that she is vulnerable to Warp.
*[[Raclesa (Uber Rare Cat)|Raclesa type Σ]]: A near-perfect fit. She's Strong Against Bahamut with comparable DPS to Kai and outranges his base attacks, surviving the Explosions for a good while if boosted. The real kicker is her Slow. Its uptime is 79.2%, keeping him from attacking (even longer if she gets a knockback with it) while you deal with the Shibalien Elite waves.
*[[High Lord Babel (Legend Rare Cat)|High Lord Babel]]: A similar story to Kai, his insanely high health (2,142,000 HP against Floating at Lv.30) makes him an absolute wall against Awakened Bahamut, and his higher range keeps him safer from being Warped by Shibalien Elite, but his cooldown and price are insanely high.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]]: Cosmo has the range to simply ignore Awakened Bahamut Cat's Explosions, allowing him to crowd-control and slowly chip Awakened Bahamut Cat from afar with ease. However, he is evidently fragile. Only send him out after Bahamut meets your frontline.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]]: Sporting insanely high range (720) and damage, his abilities will prove useful to beating both Awakened Bahamut and the Shibalien Elites, as the latter doesn't spawn too frequently, allowing Lufalan to direct most of its firepower against Bahamut. However, do note that unless CC units are used to keep Bahamut at bay, Lufalan will easily perish and its long cooldown would effectively prevent another deployment for the rest of the stage, or worse, result in a loss with the sudden drop in DPS.
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]]: She only barely outranges Awakened Bahamut's final Explosion by 25, but it's enough to damage both Bahamut and nuke Shibalien Elite with her Massive Damage ability against Aliens.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: A similar case with Aphrodite, though Phonoa is at an even higher risk due to their speed causing them to clip. But in return, they're able to tear through Awakened Bahamut even better.
*[[Tekachi (Uber Rare Cat)|Adamankachi]]: Since he targets both Floating and Alien, he can stall Awakened Bahamut and the Shibaliens for a little bit.

